     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">On Thursday, 24 December 2015 01:19:54 UTC+2, Sol Lago  wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<div><br></div><div>I am running into a problem since I updated ggplot2 to version 2.0.0. </div><div><br></div><div>Before, I normally calculated standard error bars using <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">stat_summary</font> with <b><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">mean_cl_normal</font> </b>with <b><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">mult=1</font> </b>(see <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19258460/standard-error-bars-using-stat-summary\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19258460/standard-error-bars-using-stat-summary&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368382101000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Dn9bdRlR2bA_sLSZZdcqr\">here</a> for rationale). However, since I updated ggplot2, this yields and error: </div><div><br></div><div><div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">ggplot(df, aes(x=condition, y=rt, fill=condition)) +</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">  stat_summary(fun.y = mean, geom = &quot;bar&quot;, colour=&quot;black&quot;,size=.3) + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">  stat_summary(fun.data = mean_cl_normal, mult = 1, geom = &quot;errorbar&quot;)</font></div><div style=\"color:rgb(255,0,0)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">Error in print(ggplot(df, aes(x = condition, y = amplitude, colour = condition)) +  : </font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">  error in evaluating the argument &#39;x&#39; in selecting a method for function &#39;print&#39;: Error: Unknown parameters: mult</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>Any ideas of what the problem is? And if setting <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">mult</font> is no longer an option in ggplot2, do you know of any quick way of calculating error bars that does not involve pre-averaging my data frame before creating a plot? </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a bunch!</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\"></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5BIG1vcmUgZ2VuZXJhbCBhbnN3ZXI6IGluIGdnbG90MiAyLjAuMCB0aGUgYXJndW1lbnRz\r\nIHRvIHRoZSBmdW5jdGlvbiBgZnVuLmRhdGFgIGFyZSBubyBsb25nZXIgcGFzc2VkIHRocm91Z2gg\r\nYC4uLmAgYnV0IGluc3RlYWQgYXMgYSBsaXN0IHRocm91Z2ggZm9ybWFsIHBhcmFtZXRlciBgZnVu\r\nLmFyZ3NgLiBUaGUgY29kZSBiZWxvdyBpcyB0aGUgZXhhY3QgZXF1aXZhbGVudCB0byB0aGF0IGlu\r\nIHRoZSBvcmlnaW5hbCBxdWVzdGlvbi48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj5gYGB7cn08ZGl2Pjxk\r\naXY+PGZvbnQgY29sb3I9IiMwMDAwMDAiIGZhY2U9ImNvdXJpZXIgbmV3LCBtb25vc3BhY2UiPmdn\r\ncGxvdChkZiwgYWVzKHg9Y29uZGl0aW9uLCB5PXJ0LCBmaWxsPWNvbmRpdGlvbikpICs8L2ZvbnQ+\r\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48Zm9udCBjb2xvcj0iIzAwMDAwMCIgZmFjZT0iY291cmllciBuZXcsIG1vbm9z\r\ncGFjZSI+Jm5ic3A7IHN0YXRfc3VtbWFyeShmdW4ueSA9IG1lYW4sIGdlb20gPSAiYmFyIiwgY29s\r\nb3VyPSJibGFjayIsc2l6ZT0uMykgKyZuYnNwOzwvZm9udD48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxmb250IGNvbG9y\r\nPSIjMDAwMDAwIiBmYWNlPSJjb3VyaWVyIG5ldywgbW9ub3NwYWNlIj4mbmJzcDsgc3RhdF9zdW1t\r\nYXJ5KGZ1bi5kYXRhID0gbWVhbl9jbF9ub3JtYWwsIGZ1bi5hcmdzID0gbGlzdChtdWx0ID0gMSks\r\nIGdlb20gPSAiZXJyb3JiYXIiKTwvZm9udD48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmBgYDxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pm9y\r\nIHVzaW5nIGNvZGUgdGhhdCBjYW4gYmUgcnVuOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+YGBg\r\ne3J9PC9kaXY+PGRpdj48ZGl2PmQgJmx0Oy0gZ2dwbG90KG10Y2FycywgYWVzKGN5bCwgbXBnKSkg\r\nKyBnZW9tX3BvaW50KCk8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmQgKyBzdGF0X3N1bW1hcnkoZnVuLmRhdGEgPSAiPHNw\r\nYW4gc3R5bGU9ImNvbG9yOiByZ2IoMCwgMCwgMCk7IGZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiAnY291cmllciBuZXcn\r\nLCBtb25vc3BhY2U7Ij5tZWFuX2NsX25vcm1hbDwvc3Bhbj4